Spec: TenantRestoreCmd

Purpose:
  Back the `agent tenant restore` sub-command: build the Rhai engine over the
    package, config, tenant and lib resolver directories, inject the parsed CLI
    flags as the script variable `args`, then hand the whole restore work to the
    Rhai module `restore`. This file reads and touches nothing else: no
    @TenantInstance fetch, no @set_tenant, no `instance` binding, no `context`
    module call, no `status` write, no cluster call and no restore artifact at
    all — a pure synchronous handoff. Diff-verified twin of
    ./../service/restore.rs: a real `diff` of the two 93-line sources shows
    exactly one hunk, the kind segment `{script_dir}/tenant` over
    `{script_dir}/service` in the third search directory; and of ./backup.rs it
    differs only at the two doc-comment words of the `namespace` and `instance`
    flags (`to backup` → `to restore`) and at the fixed snippet, where the
    module name is `restore` in all three positions. The flag block is
    ./install.sdd's ten-flag shape verbatim — restore adds no snapshot-id,
    destination or repository flag; the snapshot and the restic repository
    arrive script-side as process environment, never as CLI surface.

References:
  ./backup.sdd — the same-kind sibling whose body this file duplicates minus
    the snippet module name and the two doc-comment words; the frozen notes
    there (sync posture, flag-carried-unread, Dynamic discard, kind asymmetry)
    mirror here.
  ./../service/restore.sdd — the governing cross-kind twin spec for the
    diff-verified identical surface; its Tasks hold the open `[?]` decisions
    (cross-ref in the single task below).
  ./install.sdd, ./delete.sdd — the fetch-CR-plus-`context`-script shape this
    lane deliberately drops; their open flag-contract tasks mirror here.

Depends on:
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — @Script::new resolver semantics and live
    registration set, @Script::eval error lane, @Script::set_dynamic (the
    Deref'd core writer over the persistent @rhai::Scope), @Dynamic discard.
  /common/src/lib.sdd — @common::Error variants, @common::Result and the
    @common::DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE default of `agent_image`.
  @clap @Args, @serde, @serde_json — flag parsing (flags, envs, defaults below)
    and the derives behind the `args` JSON.
  /agent/scripts/tenant/restore.rhai — the runtime handoff target the snippet
    imports as `restore` under the default `--script-dir`; owned instead by
    /agent/agent.sdd. Its `run` assembles the whole restore context script-side
    through the lib module's `backup_context::from_args`: restic repository from
    `BASE_REPO_URL`/`SUB_PATH`, the snapshot to restore from `RESTIC_SNAPSHOT`,
    scale and database targets from `DEPLOYMENT_LIST`, `STATEFULSET_LIST`,
    `SECRET_LIST`, `PG_LIST`, `MYSQL_LIST`, `MONGO_LIST`, `REDIS_LIST`, plus
    `RESTIC_TAGS`, the `RESTIC_MAX_*` retention envs, `SCALE_TARGET` and
    `INSECURE_TLS` — none of these names a CLI flag; unset envs resolve to
    empty by the core @get_env. Its stage sequence (maintenance_start,
    restore_run, custom-shell and secret/database stages, maintenance_stop)
    adds the tenant-only `restore_mongodb` and `restore_redis` stages over the
    service twin's set.
  ./mod.rs — the only caller: @context::init_k8s call (an inert no-op per
    /common/src/context.sdd), then this arm's `unwrap_or_else` error lane
    (tracing text and @process::exit(5), frozen by ./mod.sdd).

Exposes:
  @Parameters — clap @Args struct, also deriving @Debug, @Serialize and
    @Deserialize; mounted by @tenant::Commands::Restore in ./mod.rs; all ten
    fields private to this module, reached only by the derive code and by @run.
  @run — @pub fn @run(@args: @&@Parameters) -> @common::Result<@()> — a plain
    non-async function (unlike the awaited install and delete twins per
    ./mod.sdd); the sole caller is @tenant::run (restore dispatch arm).

Accepts:
  @Parameters.namespace — `-n` / `--namespace`, env `NAMESPACE`, value name
    `NAMESPACE`, @String, required (no `default_value`); its doc comment is one
    of the two words making the ./backup.rs twin delta; forwarded only — never
    read by this file (contrast ./install.sdd where it keys the CR fetch).
  @Parameters.instance — `-i` / `--instance`, env `INSTANCE`, value name
    `INSTANCE`, @String, required; likewise forwarded but never read — the name
    of a @TenantInstance is never looked up here.
  @Parameters.vynil_namespace — `-v` / `--vynil-namespace`, env
    `VYNIL_NAMESPACE`, value name `VYNIL_NAMESPACE`, @String, required; never
    read beyond serialization into `args`.
  @Parameters.package_dir — `-p` / `--package-dir`, env `PACKAGE_DIRECTORY`,
    value name `PACKAGE_DIRECTORY`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default
    `/tmp/package`; read only to interpolate the first search directory.
  @Parameters.script_dir — `-s` / `--script-dir`, env `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, value
    name `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default
    `./agent/scripts`; read only to interpolate the `tenant` and `lib` search
    directories.
  @Parameters.template_dir — `-t` / `--template-dir`, env `TEMPLATE_DIRECTORY`,
    value name `TEMPLATE_DIRECTORY`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default
    `./agent/templates`; present install-shape flag, read by nothing here or by
    the snippet as evaluated.
  @Parameters.agent_image — long-only `--agent-image`, env `AGENT_IMAGE`, value
    name `AGENT_IMAGE`, @String, clap default @common::DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE, i.e.
    `docker.io/sebt3/vynil-agent:0.7.7`; the other borrowed install-shape flag
    with no reader in this lane.
  @Parameters.tag — long-only `--tag`, env `TAG`, value name `TAG`, @String,
    required; carried by the install flag shape, never parsed or used here.
  @Parameters.config_dir — `-c` / `--config-dir`, env `CONFIG_DIR`, value name
    `CONFIG_DIR`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `.`; read to interpolate the
    second search directory.
  @Parameters.controller_values — long-only `--controller-values`, env
    `CONTROLLER_VALUES`, value name `CONTROLLER_VALUES`, @String, clap default
    the two-character string `{}`.
  Runtime posture: invoked as a normal call from inside @tenant::run's async
    task, so the whole script run executes on — and blocks — one tokio worker
    thread; no runtime preconditions attach to this file (it touches no
    @context state), in contrast to ./install.sdd whose @set_tenant demands a
    multi-thread runtime.

Returns:
  @Ok(@()) once the fixed eval snippet completes without a Rhai error — the
    @Dynamic value the snippet returns is discarded by `let _ =`, never
    inspected, so @Ok means only "the script ran to end".

Raises:
  @common::Error::SerializationError (Display `SerializationError: <serde
    text>`) from the explicit @map_err when @serde_json::to_value(@Parameters)
    fails on the derives; the only fallible step before the eval.
  @common::Error::Core (wrapping @vynil_core::Error::RhaiError, Display
    `Rhai script error: <rhai text>`) from the `?` on @Script::eval — a parse
    error in the fixed snippet, a failed `restore` import in every search
    directory, or any parse error / thrown error inside the `restore` module and
    whatever it imports or import_runs.
  Never @common::Error::KubeError, never the @panic! `cannot create the
    Kubernetes client: {e}` of /common/src/context.sdd from Rust: this file
    makes no cluster call, so no kube failure can originate here (contrast
    ./install.sdd, where a missing CR is the first fallible step). Such panics
    can still arrive only through registered functions a script itself calls
    during the eval; a Rust panic there is not a catchable script error and
    unwinds through this synchronous frame into the untouched-to-panics posture
    frozen by ./mod.sdd.

Handles:
  @Err lane owned by the caller — @tenant::run logs `Restore of a package
    failed with:` followed by the error Display through @tracing::error and
    calls @process::exit(5); this file logs nothing and never exits.
  Process context never set — no @set_* runs in this lane, so the
    @VynilContext stays @VynilContext::None throughout and the script-visible
    `vynil_owner()` answers its empty map (per /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd);
    the restore context the scripts use comes from their own env-variable
    assembly, not from this process.
  Missing or gone @TenantInstance — invisible here by construction: with no
    fetch, the instance's existence cannot fail this lane; any behavior
    tolerance to a missing instance is script-side (contrast ./delete.sdd's
    hard exit-3 failure).
  Absent resolver directories — the four search paths are never existence-
    checked at construction; the failure only lands later as the
    @common::Error::Core import error if no search dir holds `restore.rhai`.
  Thrown script failures — a stage's `throw` (the shipped module throws on a
    non-zero custom-script return code) arrives as the same @Err(@Core) with
    the thrown text behind the `Rhai script error: ` prefix and rides the
    exit-5 lane.
  Restore artifacts — none in the Rust lane: the restic restore, maintenance
    toggles, secret reloads and database re-seeds are all Rhai stage work; this
    file produces no artifact and writes nothing to disk or cluster.

Must:
  Execute these steps in this order, with nothing between them: build the
    interpreter, serialize and inject `args`, evaluate the snippet, return
    @Ok — there is no fetch, publish or `instance`-inject step and none may be
    inserted; only @Parameters.package_dir, @Parameters.config_dir and
    @Parameters.script_dir are read by this file at all.
  Build the interpreter with @Script::new on exactly four resolver directories
    in this order: `{package_dir}/scripts`, `{config_dir}` (the directory
    itself), `{script_dir}/tenant`, `{script_dir}/lib` — plain string
    interpolation of @std::path::Display, so a path argument ending in `/`
    doubles the separator; earlier entries win an `import`; the `tenant` kind
    segment is hard-coded.
  @Script::new brings the full live-cluster registration set — the same one
    ./install.sdd and ./delete.sdd get (@tenant_rhai_register and the other
    two kinds, http, s3, the jukebox and the k8s registrars), so the scripts
    could self-fetch cluster state through registered bridges even though the
    Rust lane never does.
  Serialize @Parameters with @serde_json::to_value and inject it through
    @Script::set_dynamic as the script variable named `args`; the JSON object
    carries the ten declared snake_case keys `namespace`, `instance`,
    `vynil_namespace`, `package_dir`, `script_dir`, `template_dir`,
    `agent_image`, `tag`, `config_dir`, `controller_values` — install's exact
    key set — with `controller_values` as a JSON string (its default renders
    `"{}"`, still a string, not an object), `agent_image` as a string and the
    @PathBufs as path text.
  Evaluate the fixed two-statement snippet, nothing configurable in it:
    `import("restore") as restore; restore::run(args);` — the only module name
    the Rust lane names is `restore` (no `context` module, no `instance`
    argument); the trailing `;` makes the result @rhai::Dynamic::UNIT,
    discarded by `let _ =` while a failed evaluation still propagates through
    `?`.
  Keep @run non-async: @tenant::run calls it without awaiting (frozen
    discipline in ./mod.sdd), and the synchronous call blocks its tokio worker
    for the full duration of the script run.
  Emit no log and no stdout/stderr.

Must not:
  Copy the install/delete fetch shape: no @TenantInstance::get call, no
    @set_tenant, no `instance` or `context` binding here — a Rust-side read
    would fabricate a KubeError (and a panic lane) the restore Job does not
    have and would move script-side context assembly into this handoff.
  Read `template_dir`, `agent_image`, `tag` or `controller_values` to steer
    this lane, or gate on their contents: they are invisible to this file by
    shape and reach the scripts only through `args`.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover all six Scenarios with tests; no test invokes this @run — the
      module is private in @tenant so tests cannot even name it, and the only
      related coverage is tenant-flavored and script-side:
      /agent/tests/rhai_backup_redis.rs builds mock engines over the `lib` and
      `tenant` script dirs and exercises the restore-stage module
      `restore_redis` directly, bypassing this Rust lane (same posture as
      ./backup.sdd's open coverage task).
  [?] Twin-mirrored open questions — the sync-vs-async freeze, the
      snapshot-and-destination-by-environment contract (no snapshot, repository
      or destination flag in the ten), the required-but-unread flags, the
      `controller_values` JSON string, the discarded eval @Dynamic, the inert
      `restore_pre`/`restore_post` hook points (no such module ships in any
      search dir), the system-kind restore asymmetry and the @Deserialize
      derive with no deserialization site — are all unresolved in
      ./../service/restore.sdd Tasks on the diff-verified identical surface;
      keep those decisions in lockstep there rather than re-deciding here.

Done when:
  The six Scenarios hold under tests pinning the four-dir resolver order with
    the `tenant` segment, the ten-key `args` JSON with
    `template_dir`/`agent_image`/`tag` present at their defaults and
    `controller_values` as a string, the never-touches-the-cluster posture, and
    the error-to-exit(5) lane.

Scenario: full run hands off without touching the cluster
  Given all required flags supplied (by flag or env) and `restore.rhai`
    resolvable under `{script_dir}/tenant`
  When @run is called synchronously from @tenant::run
  Then @Script::new received the four search dirs `[package]/scripts`,
    `[config]`, `[script]/tenant`, `[script]/lib` in that order
  And only `args` is bound — no `instance` variable was injected and
    @set_tenant never ran, so @VynilContext stays @VynilContext::None
  Then the `restore` module's `run` executes with that args map and @run
    returns @Ok(()) whatever the discarded @Dynamic was
  And no @kube call and no file mutation originated from this file

Scenario: install-shape flags reach scripts at their defaults
  Given a command line that sets `--namespace`, `--instance`,
    `--vynil-namespace` and `--tag` but omits every defaulted flag
  When @run serializes @Parameters into `args`
  Then the object holds exactly the ten keys `namespace`, `instance`,
    `vynil_namespace`, `package_dir`, `script_dir`, `template_dir`,
    `agent_image`, `tag`, `config_dir`, `controller_values`
  And `package_dir` is `/tmp/package`, `script_dir` is `./agent/scripts`,
    `template_dir` is `./agent/templates`, `agent_image` is
    `docker.io/sebt3/vynil-agent:0.7.7`, `config_dir` is `.` and
    `controller_values` is the JSON string `"{}"`

Scenario: missing instance CR is invisible to this lane
  Given no @TenantInstance exists at the given namespace/name, the cluster is
    unreachable, and yet `restore.rhai` plus what it imports resolve and
    complete
  When @run is called
  Then @run returns @Ok(()) — @common::Error::KubeError cannot arise because no
    lookup is performed
  And the exit-5 lane is never entered

Scenario: restore module missing fails the eval
  Given valid flags but no `restore.rhai` resolvable in any of the four
    resolver directories
  When @run evaluates the snippet
  Then @Script::eval returns @Err(@common::Error::Core Display-prefixed
    `Rhai script error:`) and @run propagates it unchanged
  And @tenant::run logs `Restore of a package failed with:` carrying that text
    at @tracing::error level and exits the process 5

Scenario: thrown stage failure rides the exit-5 lane
  Given `restore.rhai` resolves and one stage throws inside the module (the
    shipped tenant module throws when a package-provided `restore.sh`,
    `restore_prepare.sh`, `restore_secret.sh`, `restore_postgresql.sh`,
    `restore_mysql.sh`, `restore_mongodb.sh` or `restore_redis.sh` returns
    non-zero)
  When @run evaluates the snippet
  Then the returned @Err(@Core) Display is `Rhai script error: ` followed by
    the thrown text
  And the exit-5 lane logs it and exits 5, with the process context still
    @VynilContext::None

Scenario: missing required flag never reaches Rust logic
  Given `--instance` omitted and `INSTANCE` unset in the environment — same
    lane for `--namespace` / `NAMESPACE`, `--vynil-namespace` /
    `VYNIL_NAMESPACE` and `--tag` / `TAG`
  When the binary parses @Parameters
  Then clap exits with its usage error before @run starts — no interpreter is
    built, and the exit-5 restore lane is never entered
